#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:34
msgid "Update a checklist requirement"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:35
msgid "Patch one discovered task for one post type using its latest hash. Supports native rule, ranges, selectors, role exceptions and labels. Preserves other tasks and post types. Native validation runs without simulated admin forms; dry_run previews without saving."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:44
msgid "Update several checklist requirements"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:45
msgid "Validate every explicit task/post-type target before one native configuration write. Each target needs its current hash. Preserves omitted configuration and accepts dry_run. Does not change post content or mark tasks completed."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:55
msgid "Create or update a custom checklist task"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:56
msgid "Create a custom checkbox or OpenAI instruction task for one supported post type, disabled by default, or patch a discovered existing task using its latest hash. New IDs are generated by the plugin. OpenAI tasks configure instructions only; this action does not call an AI service or certify its result."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:69
msgid "Remove a custom checklist task"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:70
msgid "Remove a verified custom or OpenAI task from one post type using its latest hash. Other post types and historic post completion metadata are retained. Native built-in tasks are disabled through their rule rather than deleted. dry_run checks only."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:79
msgid "Reorder checklist tasks"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:80
msgid "Move discovered requirements into the supplied native shared order. Rule ordering is shared by post types, so this can change their default task ordering too; Appearance Priority/Alphabetical modes still apply. Uses one requirement hash from the current configuration. dry_run previews without saving."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:90
msgid "Reset renamed checklist labels"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Requirements.php:91
msgid "Reset native WP Admin and Editing screen task labels to their defaults. This affects all tasks/post types, preserves task titles/rules and requires manage_options. Use checklist_hash from get-plugin-settings; dry_run checks only."
msgstr ""

